  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656076",
      "title": "Binding to Custom Events",
      "lectureOrder": 392,
      "videoOrder": 362,
      "sourceHash": "58fed2c0e76f462551eb38fad2ec16156c82b33b9873688a94b5623c4f657516",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.43,
          "end": 4.53,
          "en": "-: Great, in the last lectures,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.53,
          "end": 7.68,
          "en": "we learned something crucial, something we will use a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.68,
          "end": 11.79,
          "en": "in our demo app and this course, and probably in any app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.79,
          "end": 14.64,
          "en": "how to pass data from a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.64,
          "end": 18.12,
          "en": "down to another component which was implemented there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.12,
          "end": 20.64,
          "en": "Now about the upper direction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.64,
          "end": 24.27,
          "en": "what if we have a component and something changes in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.27,
          "end": 26.94,
          "en": "and we want to inform our parent component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.94,
          "end": 30.06,
          "en": "so the component which implements the other component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.06,
          "end": 32.46,
          "en": "For example, here in app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.46,
          "end": 34.59,
          "en": "we're implementing app cockpit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.59,
          "end": 37.89,
          "en": "and in this child component in app cockpit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.89,
          "end": 40.5,
          "en": "something can change because here we got two buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.5,
          "end": 43.17,
          "en": "and when we click the buttons we want to do something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.17,
          "end": 45.93,
          "en": "And right now the code which would normally get executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.93,
          "end": 48.3,
          "en": "was simply commented out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.3,
          "end": 51.87,
          "en": "So here, we want to inform our parent component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.87,
          "end": 54.24,
          "en": "the app component in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.24,
          "end": 58.023,
          "en": "that a new server or a new blueprint was created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.95,
          "end": 62.61,
          "en": "So in our app component, we may still want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.61,
          "end": 65.19,
          "en": "implement these two methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.19,
          "end": 68.91,
          "en": "So that simply add them here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.91,
          "end": 72.53999999999999,
          "en": "However, I will adjust the names and say onServerAdded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.5,
          "end": 76.95,
          "en": "Because these methods will only be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.95,
          "end": 79.32,
          "en": "after this button has been clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.32,
          "end": 82.38,
          "en": "So not once the button's clicked, but thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.38,
          "end": 85.65,
          "en": "Once we really already are done creating the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.65,
          "end": 86.91,
          "en": "so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.91,
          "end": 90.51,
          "en": "So onServerAdded and onBlueprintAdded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.51,
          "end": 94.8,
          "en": "sound like more appropriate names here in the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.8,
          "end": 97.77000000000001,
          "en": "Then however we can comment out this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.77000000000001,
          "end": 101.37,
          "en": "and still create a new server or a new blueprint.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.37,
          "end": 106.37,
          "en": "However, this will not work as expected here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.59,
          "end": 109.17,
          "en": "because we're referencing new server's name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.17,
          "end": 111.33,
          "en": "and new server content which are not available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.33,
          "end": 112.62,
          "en": "in the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.62,
          "end": 116.34,
          "en": "But that is exactly information we kind of want to pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.34,
          "end": 118.8,
          "en": "from the cockpit to the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.8,
          "end": 121.59,
          "en": "Because the app component is the central place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.59,
          "end": 125.79,
          "en": "in our app for now, which manages this array of service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.79,
          "end": 128.82,
          "en": "So how can we emit an event, our own event?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.82,
          "end": 132.21,
          "en": "How can we inform our app component?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.21,
          "end": 135.21,
          "en": "It would be great if it would look something like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.21,
          "end": 136.59,
          "en": "on the app cockpit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.59,
          "end": 139.05,
          "en": "So in the app component html file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.05,
          "end": 141.96,
          "en": "where we implement app cockpit, it would be great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.96,
          "end": 146.22,
          "en": "if we could listen to serverCreated, any name you like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.22,
          "end": 147.45,
          "en": "but that would be a fitting name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.45,
          "end": 149.79,
          "en": "for the kind of event we want to listen to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.79,
          "end": 152.64,
          "en": "Of course this event doesn't exist by default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.64,
          "end": 154.11,
          "en": "So just like we listened to click,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.11,
          "end": 154.94299999999998,
          "en": "now we want to listen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.94299999999998,
          "end": 157.62,
          "en": "to some event like this, serverCreated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.62,
          "end": 160.89,
          "en": "And once our server was created, we execute some code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 160.89,
          "end": 164.61,
          "en": "So just like in any other build-in event like Click,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.61,
          "end": 167.04,
          "en": "here on the rights of the equal sign",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 167.04,
          "end": 168.36,
          "en": "between the quotation marks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.36,
          "end": 170.94,
          "en": "we want to call onServerAdded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 170.94,
          "end": 172.89,
          "en": "the method we prepared for this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 172.89,
          "end": 176.333,
          "en": "And we even expect to get some data with $event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 176.333,
          "end": 178.86,
          "en": "This is how you could catch this data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 178.86,
          "end": 181.62,
          "en": "That could be some object which gives us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 181.62,
          "end": 184.44,
          "en": "the required information about that server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 184.44,
          "end": 186.003,
          "en": "like the name and the content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 186.84,
          "end": 189.81,
          "en": "So in onServerAdded now here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 189.81,
          "end": 192.99,
          "en": "we would expect to get event data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 192.99,
          "end": 195.57,
          "en": "or let's say we would actually expect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 195.57,
          "end": 199.35,
          "en": "to get the server data, and that could be of type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 199.35,
          "end": 202.14,
          "en": "let's say a JavaScript object which has a name field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 202.14,
          "end": 203.73,
          "en": "with a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 203.73,
          "end": 205.38,
          "en": "or let's be more explicit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 205.38,
          "end": 209.55,
          "en": "let's name it serverName, which is of type string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 209.55,
          "end": 213.15,
          "en": "and serverContent, which is of type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 213.15,
          "end": 216.45,
          "en": "So that would be the type of object we expect to get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 216.45,
          "end": 217.82999999999998,
          "en": "in this method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 217.82999999999998,
          "end": 220.98,
          "en": "And with that, we could use it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 220.98,
          "end": 225.98,
          "en": "and use serverData, serverName to assign it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 226.26,
          "end": 228.357,
          "en": "as a name for our newly created server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 228.357,
          "end": 231.06,
          "en": "the one we push onto our array here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 231.06,
          "end": 235.11,
          "en": "And the same of course down here for the content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 235.11,
          "end": 238.23,
          "en": "So that is how it should work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 238.23,
          "end": 242.7,
          "en": "We get this data in onServerAdded, and we call onServerAdded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 242.7,
          "end": 246.87,
          "en": "once our custom event occurs on the cockpit component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 246.87,
          "end": 248.94,
          "en": "And this event even should give us this data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 248.94,
          "end": 252.273,
          "en": "we expect to get, and we catch it with $event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 253.47,
          "end": 258.36,
          "en": "Now obviously we can also replicate this for the let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 258.36,
          "end": 263.28,
          "en": "bluePrintCreated event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 263.28,
          "end": 265.98,
          "en": "Here we would execute onBlueprintAdded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 265.98,
          "end": 268.38,
          "en": "and of course you could also merge these two methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 268.38,
          "end": 270.36,
          "en": "I keep them separate to be really clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 270.36,
          "end": 272.04,
          "en": "about what's happening here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 272.04,
          "end": 275.73,
          "en": "And there again, we also expect to get our,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 275.73,
          "end": 278.7,
          "en": "well, blueprint data in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 278.7,
          "end": 281.49,
          "en": "So blueprintData maybe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 281.49,
          "end": 286.49,
          "en": "And there we also would receive the information we require",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 287.61,
          "end": 292.503,
          "en": "like the server name and then of course also the content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 294.48,
          "end": 296.1,
          "en": "This is how it should work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 296.1,
          "end": 298.68,
          "en": "Now in the cockpit component, we actually need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 298.68,
          "end": 301.05,
          "en": "to emit our own event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 301.05,
          "end": 304.167,
          "en": "We are waiting for events named serverCreated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 304.167,
          "end": 308.31,
          "en": "and bluePrintCreated, maybe with a lowercase P.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 308.31,
          "end": 312.81,
          "en": "So in the cockpit component, I want to create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 312.81,
          "end": 316.563,
          "en": "two new properties here, properties that's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 317.405,
          "end": 322.405,
          "en": "ServerCreated and blueprintCreated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 322.47,
          "end": 325.8,
          "en": "Now before we placed @ input in front of them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 325.8,
          "end": 330.033,
          "en": "to mark them as properties you can set from outside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 330.87,
          "end": 332.97,
          "en": "Now we want to do the opposite.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 332.97,
          "end": 335.90999999999997,
          "en": "We want to make sure that both properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 335.90999999999997,
          "end": 338.49,
          "en": "are events we can emit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 338.49,
          "end": 340.40999999999997,
          "en": "And to make them events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 340.40999999999997,
          "end": 344.19,
          "en": "we first of all have to assign a new value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 344.19,
          "end": 349.19,
          "en": "new EventEmitter, and EventEmitter needs to be imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 349.53,
          "end": 351.09000000000003,
          "en": "from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 351.09000000000003,
          "end": 354.18,
          "en": "So you should add this import here at the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 354.18,
          "end": 356.43,
          "en": "EventEmitter is a generic type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 356.43,
          "end": 358.89,
          "en": "which is indicated in TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 358.89,
          "end": 361.59,
          "en": "by using this smaller than and greater than sign.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 361.59,
          "end": 363.96,
          "en": "And in between you simply define the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 363.96,
          "end": 366.87,
          "en": "of event data you're going to emit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 366.87,
          "end": 369.69,
          "en": "And here, well we know this will just be the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 369.69,
          "end": 371.52,
          "en": "we expect to the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 371.52,
          "end": 373.74,
          "en": "So this will be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 373.74,
          "end": 375.96,
          "en": "with a serverName and serverContent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 375.96,
          "end": 379.08,
          "en": "So we can pass this in between these smaller",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 379.08,
          "end": 380.67,
          "en": "and greater than signs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 380.67,
          "end": 383.04,
          "en": "And important, add parenthesis in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 383.04,
          "end": 385.11,
          "en": "to call the constructor of EventEmitter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 385.11,
          "end": 387.27,
          "en": "and create a new EventEmitter object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 387.27,
          "end": 389.973,
          "en": "which is now stored in serverCreated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 391.74,
          "end": 394.89,
          "en": "I'll do the same for blueprintCreated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 394.89,
          "end": 398.04200000000003,
          "en": "Now we get two event emitters and that's the first step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 398.04200000000003,
          "end": 401.88,
          "en": "EventEmitter is an object in the angular framework",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 401.88,
          "end": 404.97,
          "en": "which allows you to emit your own events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 404.97,
          "end": 407.12,
